===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{lb|en|manner}} With depth, [[meaningfully]].
#: ''He thought and wrote '''profoundly'''.''
# {{lb|en|evaluative}} Very [[importantly]].
#: '''''More profoundly''', it has shaken our most fundamental assumptions.''
# {{lb|en|degree}} [[deeply|Deeply]]; [[very]]; [[strongly]] or [[forcefully]].
#: ''From his childhood, she was '''profoundly''' troubled.''
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=2019|author=Li Huang|author2=James Lambert|title=Another Arrow for the Quiver: A New Methodology for Multilingual Researchers|journal=Journal of Multilingual and Multicultural Development|doi=10.1080/01434632.2019.1596115|page=11|text=In fact, the influence of signage in a certain area may exist anywhere on a continuum from '''profoundly''' effective to utterly trivial or completely insignificant, irrespective of the intent motivating the signs.}}


